     "text": "{\"cost\": 8, \"rationale\": \"Shortest path: (1) phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. (2) pivot_internal gives reach_internal, since there is no segmentation. (3) auth_ciserver gives foothold_ciserver, since there is no MFA. (4) escalate_ciserver gives admin_ciserver, since the CI server is not patched. (5) leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin. (6) auth_db gives foothold_db. (7) escalate_db gives admin_db, using stolen_dbadmin. (8) exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. This cannot be shortened. Every exfiltration step needs an admin on db, fileserver or backup, which takes an auth step, an escalate step and stolen_dbadmin. Getting stolen_dbadmin needs reach_internal (a foothold plus pivot), stolen_user, and then a foothold, escalation and leak or dump on the CI server, DC or ADFS. The CI-server route is cheapest at 5 steps, giving 5 + 3 = 8. The DC or ADFS routes need extra kerberoast and auth steps, for a total of 10.\"}"
